  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream/main a6bd69d8).\n\n## What reproduced\n\nIn #1066 the planar ladder takes its first descent from the top of the cut plus the plunge height (2 mm): Pocket and Contour read their Top height, Bore reads the hole's `entry_z`. The issue suspected a rapid into stock that stands higher than that top. Fixture: a 40 x 40 x 20 part with a 20 x 20 blind hole (mouth Z 20) in a box 5 mm taller (top Z 25), nothing faced ahead. Each op's entry rapid goes from Z 40 to Z 22, 3 mm into uncut stock.\n\n- 2D Pocket, Contour, and a Bore sourced from the part: already convicted by the rapid law (#96, `RapidInStock`), and the post is blocked.\n- **A Bore sourced from the stock: no warning, and it posted.** That's a silent rapid into material, so the issue went to P0.\n\nCause: `sim::verify::rapids_in_stock` asks `Rest::in_stock`, which falls back to the op's region when `VerifyContext::stock` is `None`, and a stock-sourced op leaves it `None`. For Bore and Thread that region is the stock footprint with the holes' rims punched out, so the column inside the hole never counted as stock.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `operation::material_source::judged_stock` (new, about 20 lines): when the source is the stock and the kind is Bore or Thread, verify's column law reads the stock's own facets instead of the punched region. Every other source and kind reads exactly as before.\n- `operation::generate`: the upright and 3+2 verify readings both take that stock. No generator or path changes, so no golden moves.\n- `docs/decisions/1066-ladder-entry-height.md`: why the law's reading was fixed rather than raising the ladder's top, and the options dropped.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New suite `crates/app/tests/ladder_entry_height.rs`. Each of its 4 tests runs Pocket, Bore and Contour:\n  - `a_ladder_entry_rapid_under_a_taller_block_is_named_and_blocks_the_post`: `RapidInStock` at the entry rapid, and the post gate refuses it. It fails on main for Bore and passes with the fix; I checked both.\n  - `a_block_standing_inside_the_plunge_height_is_fed_through_silently` (1.5 mm over the mouth)\n  - `stock_to_the_mouth_is_silent_and_posts`\n  - `a_face_ahead_to_the_mouth_acquits_the_entry_rapid` (`acquit_by_prior` still clears it)\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (1 step, 43 app binaries + lib, 148 s)\n- I also ran the suites that build Bore or Thread ops: arc_entry, circular_pick, mill2d_b, mill2d_c, operations, refusal_location, level_links, vertical_arc_entry, project_roundtrip, golden_cl and conformance. All green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The Thread case is covered by the same `matches!` arm but has no pinning test of its own (its entry is judged by #992's thread-entry law).\n- The 3+2 (tilted) reading takes the same stock, but no tilted test was run for it.\n- Drill isn't touched: its R-plane law already refuses this case at generate (checked on the same fixture).\n\nChangelog: A milled Bore sourced from the stock now has its entry rapid judged against the stock above the hole's mouth: a rapid into uncut stock is named and blocks the post (#1066)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1066\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
